  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. We have strong evidence that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the optimal architecture, and that resnet50 ≈ imagenet_vit_l. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as pca_n2000 across all multimodal experiments. Question: config_031 is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding the best-known architecture (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) constant. This directly tests whether a learned, biologically-informed RNA representation (scVI) can outperform a linear PCA projection in the multimodal setting. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a fundamental, high-impact design choice that remains completely unexplored in multimodal settings. A positive result would open a productive new search direction (scvi/scgpt encoders); a null result would confirm PCA sufficiency and let us focus remaining budget on other axes. This is more informative than testing transformer+weighted (where avgpool's ~4% advantage over transformer with concat makes a reversal unlikely) or re-testing image encoder variants (already shown to be near-equivalent)."
}

